md`# Cloud Brain: specification`
// %%
opening = md`A Cloud Brain is a set of Cloudflare Workers that one owner controls. Each Worker is deployed from one module of this notebook. A deployer Worker holds the only Cloudflare token and does every deploy. An assistant in a browser tab answers messages. No Worker calls a model.

This module says what must be true and how each statement is checked. \`@tomlarkworthy/cloud-brain-docs\` says how the Brain works. The build record at the end of this module says what was run and what came back.

Rewritten 2026-10-07 against the seeds in \`tools/cloud-brain/\`. The version before it is \`plan/specs/cloud-brain.html\` in the repository.`
// %%
related = htl.html`<p>Open: ${["cloud-brain-docs", "cloud-brain"].map((n, i) => htl.html`${i ? " · " : ""}<a href=${linkTo("@tomlarkworthy/" + n, { onObservable: false })} onclick=${(e) => (e.preventDefault(), navigate(e.currentTarget.getAttribute("href")))}><code>${n}</code></a>`)}</p>`
// %%
readiness = {
  const notes = (annotations || []).filter((a) => a.home === specModule || (a.anchor && a.anchor.module === specModule));
  const unchecked = requirements.filter((r) => !r.check || /^<.*>$/.test(r.check.trim()));
  const blocking = questions.filter((q) => q.blocking && !q.answer);
  const undrawn = states.filter((s) => !s.drawing);
  const items = [
    [notes.length, "annotations to resolve"],
    [blocking.length, "blocking questions open"],
    [unchecked.length, `of ${requirements.length} requirements without a check`],
    [undrawn.length, `of ${states.length} states without a drawing`]
  ];
  const ready = items.every(([n]) => n === 0) && specStatus === "approved for handover";
  // Everything that still needs the reviewer, listed here with a link to where it is answered.
  const open = questions.map((q, i) => ({ q, i })).filter(({ q }) => !q.answer);
  const todo = [
    ...open.filter(({ q }) => q.blocking).map(({ q, i }) => ({ tag: "blocking question", text: q.q, to: `[data-question="${i}"]` })),
    ...open.filter(({ q }) => !q.blocking).map(({ q, i }) => ({ tag: "open question", text: q.q, to: `[data-question="${i}"]` })),
    ...unchecked.map((r) => ({ tag: "no check", text: `${r.id} ${r.text}`, to: `[data-requirement="${r.id}"]` })),
    ...undrawn.map((s) => ({ tag: "not drawn", text: `state: ${s.state}`, to: `[data-state="${s.state}"]` }))
  ];
  const box = htl.html`<div style="font:13px system-ui;padding:.5em .8em;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);border-radius:6px"></div>`;
  // Scrolls the pane; a plain #fragment link would replace the lopepage layout hash.
  const jump = (to) => (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    const el = (box.closest(".lp2-pane") || box.ownerDocument).querySelector(to);
    if (!el) return;
    el.scrollIntoView({ block: "center", behavior: "smooth" });
    if (el.animate) el.animate([{ background: "color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent)" }, { background: "transparent" }], 1800);
  };
  const short = (s) => (s.length > 110 ? s.slice(0, 110) + "…" : s);
  box.append(htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:1.2em;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline">
    <strong>${ready ? "Ready to hand over" : "Not ready to hand over"}</strong>
    ${items.map(([n, label]) => htl.html`<span style=${{ opacity: n ? 1 : 0.5 }}><strong>${n}</strong> ${label}</span>`)}
  </div>`);
  if (todo.length) box.append(htl.html`<ol style="margin:.5em 0 0;padding-left:1.4em">${todo.map((t) => htl.html`<li><a href="#" onclick=${jump(t.to)}>${t.tag}</a>: ${short(t.text)}</li>`)}</ol>`);
  return box;
}
// %%
md`## Review

- **Leave a note**: ☰ → Annotate → Note, then drag over the words. The build keeps a note and the status. It replaces every other cell from the seed.
- A change to a requirement, a state or a question goes in \`tools/cloud-brain/cloud-brain-specs.ojs\`.
- The 17 notes from 2026-10-04 and 2026-10-05 were deleted on 2026-10-07 (Tom: \"delete\"). The questions table has their answers.`
// %%
md`## Outcome

| | must be true | built |
|---|---|---|
| O1 | The owner deploys a service from the page. The deployer distils the module source and deploys it. | yes |
| O2 | A deploy that fails its self-test, its health check or its tests is restored with no person involved. | yes |
| O3 | A person sends a message on a channel. A turn of the assistant in a Brain tab answers on the same channel. | WhatsApp: yes. Bluesky: yes, 2 messages on cb4 2026-10-07 (the owner, a member); each entry holds a reply. The reply was not looked for in the Bluesky app. |
| O4 | A turn runs with the permissions of its sender, not of the tab. | yes |
| O5 | A member deploys a Worker that has the member's permissions and no more. | yes, with scratch members |
| O6 | With no tab open, a message waits in the inbox and the sender gets one notice an hour. | yes, under \`simulate\` (R54) |
| O7 | Another atproto account calls a method that the owner granted, through its own PDS. | claims tested; no real PDS call to this build |
| O8 | A person with a copy of the page, a Cloudflare account and a browser installs a Brain. No data is copied. | one account, 2026-10-05; not run since |
| O9 | The assistant can change a service and deploy the change. | yes, on cb1 2026-10-06 00:21 to 00:31 (the proxy changed, a new service \`brain-x-files\` deployed) and on cb3 2026-10-06 08:31 (a new service \`brain-files\`). The record holds no such run of 2026-10-07 and none on cb4. |
| O10 | A turn runs with no tab open. | no. A notebook in a Cloudflare Container is a separate workstream. |`
// %%
md`## Scope

### Not your concern

- **robocoop-5.** The assistant is robocoop-5, unchanged. The page gives it a prompt, tools and a watch.
- **\`@tomlarkworthy/exporter-3\` and \`lopecode-channel.ts\`.** Do not change them.
- **Meta and Bluesky.** The owner makes the app, the number and the account.
- **A PDS.** The Brain is a service that a PDS forwards to. It stores no atproto repository.
- **Services outside the core** (\`brain-inbox\`, \`brain-whatsapp\`, \`brain-bluesky\`, \`brain-library\`, \`brain-proxy\`). Each module holds its own rules and tests. This spec has one requirement for all channels.

### Non-goals

- An agent loop or a model call in a Worker.
- The Observable runtime in a running Worker. The deployer runs it in QuickJS to distil, and nowhere else.
- More than one owner. Other people are members.
- A copy of data on clone or install.
- A way to change the deployer from the Brain.
- Terraform or Pulumi compatibility.`
// %%
md`## Words

The page uses these strings. Read from \`cloud-brain.ojs\`, \`cloudflare-iac.ojs\` and \`brain-deployer.ojs\` on 2026-10-07.`
// %%
copy_title = md`Cloud Brain`
// %%
copy_opening = md`Read-only. Sign in as the owner to use this Brain, or use Clone below to make your own.`
// %%
copy_strings = md`| where | text |
|---|---|
| status, local copy | This is a local copy. It is not connected to a Brain. Use Clone below to make one in your Cloudflare account. |
| status, no answer | This Brain did not answer. |
| status, not the owner | Signed in as @HANDLE. This Brain belongs to someone else, so you can read it, and use Clone below to make your own. |
| status, owner | Signed in as @HANDLE, the owner of HOST. |
| sign-in | atproto handle · your-handle.bsky.social · Sign in · Sign out |
| sections | Health · Operator · Services · Library · Access · People · Clone |
| assistant line | Answering messages in this tab. · Standing by. Another tab is answering. · N waiting · Inbox: ERROR |
| service states | in sync · changed · not installed · skewed · failing · cannot deploy · unknown |
| service notes | waiting for approval · approved, press Apply · unverified: its tests have not been run from this version |
| skew note | WORKER is running HASH, which the deployer did not deploy. |
| apply | Apply N changes · Waiting for approval: WORKERS. |
| probation | NAME HASH is live on probation. Confirm within MM:SS or it is rolled back. · Keep this version |
| rolled back | NAME HASH was rolled back to HASH at TIME: REASON |
| access | New token · Grant access · Revoke · Remove · No tokens or grants. · Copy this token now. It is not shown again. |
| people | Add member · Refresh · Set · Save · Remove · Add · may deploy |
| clone | Copy the seed · Clone into my account · Download this notebook · Installed. Your Brain is at URL. · The seed Worker was deleted. |
| deployer page | Cloud Brain deployer · Waiting for approval · Roll back · Deploys need approval: on · Turn off · Recovery key |`
// %%
md`## Visual design

The six drawings are from 2026-10-04 and 2026-10-05. Their layout holds. Their row text has the old names, and they show Secrets, Add recipe and a saved state that the page does not have. Three states have no drawing.`
// %%
drawTools = {
  const tools = [["select", "Select", "V"], ["rect", "Rect", "R"], ["ellipse", "Ellipse", "E"], ["line", "Line", "L"], ["text", "Text", "T"], ["pen", "Pen", "P"], ["scribble", "Scribble", "S"]];
  let host = null;
  const drawing = () => host && [...host.querySelectorAll("svg")].find((s) => typeof s.setTool === "function");
  const hint = htl.html`<span style="opacity:.6">click a drawing, then pick a tool</span>`;
  const bar = htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;font:13px system-ui;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2;padding:.4em 0;background:var(--theme-background, #fff)"></div>`;
  for (const [id, label, key] of tools) {
    const b = htl.html`<button title="${label} (${key})">${label}</button>`;
    b.onclick = () => { const d = drawing(); if (d) d.setTool(id); else hint.textContent = "click a drawing first"; };
    bar.append(b);
  }
  bar.append(hint);
  const onDown = (e) => {
    let n = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest("svg") : null;
    while (n && typeof n.setTool !== "function") n = n.parentElement ? n.parentElement.closest("svg") : null;
    if (!n) return;
    host = n.parentElement;
    hint.textContent = "tools apply to the drawing you last clicked";
  };
  window.document.addEventListener("pointerdown", onDown, true);
  invalidation.then(() => window.document.removeEventListener("pointerdown", onDown, true));
  return bar;
}
