// %%
artboard_probation = svgLens({ keyboard: true })`<svg viewBox="0 0 640 170" width="100%" style="max-width:640px;background:var(--theme-background)" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">
  <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="24" fill="var(--theme-background-alt)"/>
  <line x1="0" y1="24" x2="640" y2="24" stroke="var(--theme-foreground-fainter)"/>
  <text x="15" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground)" text-anchor="middle">☰</text>
  <rect x="30" y="0" width="92" height="24" fill="var(--theme-background)"/>
  <text x="38" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">cloud-brain   ×</text>
  <text x="132" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground-muted)">+</text>
  <text x="24" y="62" font-size="22" font-weight="700" font-family="Source Serif 4, Georgia, serif" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">Cloud Brain</text>
  <circle cx="29" cy="82" r="5" fill="#e6a700"/>
  <text x="42" y="86" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-foreground-muted)">kernel 9c03d7e · on probation</text>
  <rect x="24" y="102" width="592" height="46" rx="4" fill="color-mix(in srgb, #e6a700 18%, var(--theme-background))" stroke="#e6a700"/>
  <text x="36" y="122" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">New kernel 9c03d7e is live on probation.</text>
  <text x="36" y="139" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">Confirm within 08:41 or it is rolled back.</text>
  <rect x="484" y="110" width="120" height="30" rx="5" fill="var(--theme-foreground-focus)"/>
  <text x="544" y="130" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-background)" text-anchor="middle">Keep this version</text>
</svg>`
// %%
md`**probation**: shown from the moment a new kernel, core, \`brain-db\` or page is live. The countdown reads the deployer's deadline.`
// %%
artboard_rolled_back = svgLens({ keyboard: true })`<svg viewBox="0 0 640 152" width="100%" style="max-width:640px;background:var(--theme-background)" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">
  <rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="24" fill="var(--theme-background-alt)"/>
  <line x1="0" y1="24" x2="640" y2="24" stroke="var(--theme-foreground-fainter)"/>
  <text x="15" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground)" text-anchor="middle">☰</text>
  <rect x="30" y="0" width="92" height="24" fill="var(--theme-background)"/>
  <text x="38" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">cloud-brain   ×</text>
  <text x="132" y="16" font-size="11" fill="var(--theme-foreground-muted)">+</text>
  <text x="24" y="62" font-size="22" font-weight="700" font-family="Source Serif 4, Georgia, serif" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">Cloud Brain</text>
  <circle cx="29" cy="82" r="5" fill="#2e9e5b"/>
  <text x="42" y="86" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-foreground-muted)">kernel 4f2a91c · confirmed 3 days ago</text>
  <rect x="24" y="102" width="592" height="30" rx="4" fill="color-mix(in srgb, #e5484d 18%, var(--theme-background))" stroke="#e5484d"/>
  <text x="36" y="122" font-size="12" fill="var(--theme-foreground)">Kernel 9c03d7e was rolled back to 4f2a91c at 14:32: health check failed twice</text>
</svg>`
// %%
md`**rolled back**: shown until the next deploy of that Worker.`
// %%
artboard_deployer = svgLens({ keyboard: true })`<svg viewBox="0 0 640 330" width="100%" style="max-width:640px;background:#ffffff" font-family="ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace">
  <text x="24" y="40" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#111111">Cloud Brain deployer</text>
  <text x="24" y="70" font-size="12" fill="#111111">kernel:  9c03d7e  deployed 14:21  PROBATION  health FAIL FAIL</text>
  <text x="24" y="90" font-size="12" fill="#111111">last confirmed:  4f2a91c  2026-10-01 09:12</text>
  <text x="24" y="124" font-size="12" fill="#111111">Recovery key</text>
  <rect x="24" y="132" width="300" height="26" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#111111"/>
  <rect x="24" y="172" width="200" height="30" fill="#111111"/>
  <text x="124" y="192" font-size="12" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Roll back to 4f2a91c</text>
  <text x="24" y="236" font-size="12" fill="#111111">confirmed versions</text>
  <text x="24" y="256" font-size="12" fill="#444444">4f2a91c  2026-10-01 09:12   [roll back]</text>
  <text x="24" y="274" font-size="12" fill="#444444">b77e010  2026-09-28 17:40   [roll back]</text>
  <text x="24" y="292" font-size="12" fill="#444444">1d9c4aa  2026-09-27 08:03   [roll back]</text>
  <text x="24" y="316" font-size="11" fill="#777777">deployer 3 · served by brain-deployer, no kernel involved</text>
</svg>`
// %%
md`**deployer page**: \`https://BASE-deployer.SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev/\`. One HTML response, no script. Each action needs the recovery key.`
// %%
states = [
  { state: "default", drawing: "artboard_default", when: "the owner is signed in and every Worker is in sync" },
  { state: "signed out", drawing: "artboard_signed_out", when: "no session, or a session that the kernel refuses" },
  { state: "changes", drawing: "artboard_plan", when: "a Worker is changed, not installed, skewed, failing or unverified; or an apply waits for approval" },
  { state: "probation", drawing: "artboard_probation", when: "a new kernel, core, brain-db or page is live and not confirmed" },
  { state: "rolled back", drawing: "artboard_rolled_back", when: "the deployer restored the previous version" },
  { state: "deployer page", drawing: "artboard_deployer", when: "the deployer's own address" },
  { state: "local copy", drawing: "", when: "the page is opened from a file: Clone only, no Brain" },
  { state: "member", drawing: "", when: "a member is signed in: the member's services, portals, no owner panels" },
  { state: "no answer", drawing: "", when: "the Brain did not answer /auth/session" }
]
// %%
statesTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th>state</th><th>when</th><th>drawing</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${states.map((s) => htl.html`<tr data-state=${s.state}><td>${s.state}</td><td>${s.when}</td><td>${s.drawing ? htl.html`<code>${s.drawing}</code>` : htl.html`<em>not drawn</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
// %%
md`### Visual constraints

- Cells use the theme variables \`--theme-background\`, \`--theme-foreground\` and \`--theme-foreground-muted\`. Three fixed hues: green \`#2e9e5b\`, amber \`#e6a700\`, red \`#e5484d\`.
- Each control is an \`Inputs\` control (Tom, 2026-10-05: "stick to Inputs").
- The Services table is \`serviceList\` in \`cloudflare-iac\`.
- The deployer page uses no theme, no font and no script.
- Editing is off when the page opens. The ☰ menu turns it on.`
// %%
md`## Requirements

One requirement per row. **check** names the \`test_\` cells and the live run that prove it. A date and time is a run on a deployed Brain, recorded in the build record. "Not verified" says what no run has shown. A row whose check says "Not verified", "Not as required" or "No test" has the status \`part\`.

\`cb1\`, \`cb2\` and \`cb3\` were scratch Brains of 2026-10-05 and 2026-10-06 and are deleted. \`cb4\` is the Brain that runs now.`
// %%
requirements = [
  { id: "R1", status: "built", text: "cloudflare.Service(name, fn, options) must emit the function and each cell it depends on, across imports, as ES modules with no Observable runtime.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_chase, test_hash_is_stable_and_per_service" },
  { id: "R2", status: "built", text: "The emit must refuse a generator, a viewof or mutable cell, a DOM builtin and a computed secret name. The error must name the cell.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_refuses_generator, test_refuses_viewof, test_refuses_dom_builtin, test_refuses_computed_secret" },
  { id: "R3", status: "built", text: "The deployer must build a Worker's bindings from the platform cells that its code reaches. A deploy request cannot name a binding.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_bindings_follow_platform_cells. brain-deployer: test_the_table_database_is_bound_to_brain_db_alone" },
  { id: "R4", status: "built", text: "A service must answer one request the same way in the tab and as its emitted module. simulate must throw on an outbound call that has no fake.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_simulate, test_hono_same_in_tab_and_emitted, test_plain_function_caller_and_error_shape" },
  { id: "R5", status: "built", text: "Only the deployer holds a Cloudflare API token.", check: "brain-deployer: test_only_the_deployer_names_the_cloudflare_token. Cloudflare 2026-10-05: the token is a binding of BASE-deployer only" },
  { id: "R6", status: "built", text: "A deploy is module source. The deployer must distil it in QuickJS, with no network and no bindings, and must accept no Worker code.", check: "brain-deployer: test_apply_takes_source_and_deploys_what_it_distils, test_distil_answers_the_tabs_hash_and_deploys_nothing. cloudflare-iac: test_distils_in_quickjs_to_the_same_hash. Live: brain.ts redistil reports same for each Worker" },
  { id: "R7", status: "built", text: "The deployer must refuse an apply that names the deployer, an owner service whose name does not start brain-x-, and a method or path that another Worker serves.", check: "brain-deployer: test_apply_refusals, test_deployerAllows_examples, test_a_path_or_method_belongs_to_one_worker" },
  { id: "R8", status: "built", text: "When a version fails its self-test or two health checks, the deployer must restore the previous version and append an inbox entry.", check: "brain-deployer: test_failed_selftest_is_put_back, test_failing_twice_after_go_live_is_put_back. cb1 2026-10-05 22:49: restored in 35.7 s" },
  { id: "R9", status: "built", text: "A deploy is unverified until the page loads the module from the Worker, runs its test_ cells and reports. A failed report on an unverified deploy must restore the previous version.", check: "brain-core: test_a_deploy_is_unverified_until_its_tests_are_reported. brain-deployer: test_a_failed_verdict_puts_the_deploy_back" },
  { id: "R10", status: "built", text: "A new kernel, core, brain-db or page is on probation. The deployer must restore the previous version after 10 minutes with no confirm and no passed report.", check: "brain-deployer: test_kernel_probation, test_probation_transitions, test_the_page_worker_is_on_timed_probation. cb1 2026-10-05 23:35: restored by the alarm" },
  { id: "R11", status: "part", text: "When approval is on, the deployer must hold an owner apply until the owner approves it on the deployer page with the recovery key.", check: "brain-deployer: test_approval_holds_an_apply. Not as required: brain.ts apply sends the recovery key and is not held" },
  { id: "R12", status: "built", text: "With the recovery key, the deployer page must roll the kernel back when the kernel does not answer.", check: "brain-deployer: test_deployer_page_rolls_the_kernel_back, test_infra_needs_the_kernel_or_the_recovery_key. cb1 2026-10-05 23:39: 4 s" },
  { id: "R13", status: "built", text: "Each Worker must serve its manifest and its module source. A service cannot replace getInfo.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_a_worker_serves_its_manifest_and_its_source, test_getInfo_cannot_be_replaced" },
  { id: "R14", status: "built", text: "The Services list must show each Worker as in sync, changed, not installed, skewed, failing or cannot deploy. One action must apply all changed rows.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_service_rows_states" },
  { id: "R15", status: "built", text: "A deployer update must distil each Worker again from the source that the deployer keeps.", check: "brain-deployer: test_redistil_after_a_deployer_update_and_source_follows_a_put_back" },
  { id: "R16", status: "built", text: "The kernel must serve the shell at / to anyone. The shell holds no module that a Worker owns. The page must load those modules from the Workers.", check: "brain-shell: test_shellOf_cuts_the_modules_their_files_and_their_mains, test_joinModules_adds_a_module_once_and_imports_reach_it. brain-kernel: test_did_document_and_page" },
  { id: "R17", status: "built", text: "The page must open with the tabs cloud-brain, cloud-brain-docs and cloud-brain-specs. The operator prompt must name the docs module.", check: "the Brain's address with no hash: the three tabs show. cloud-brain: test_the_operator_is_told_to_read_the_docs" },
  { id: "R18", status: "part", text: "The kernel must sign a person in with atproto OAuth. The kernel must set no cookie and read no cookie. A session is a bearer token.", check: "brain-kernel: test_session_token, test_a_token_is_the_callers_to_send_from_anywhere. cb4 2026-10-07 13:47: a session sent as a cookie gets 401. Not verified: a sign-in through a PDS that ends on the callback page" },
  { id: "R19", status: "built", text: "Only the kernel's key can name a caller. The wrapper must remove each x-brain- header from a request that did not arrive over a binding.", check: "brain-kernel: test_forged_caller_is_dropped, test_credentials_are_not_forwarded. cloudflare-iac: test_only_bindings_and_the_deployer_reach_a_recipe" },
  { id: "R20", status: "built", text: "Only the kernel and the deployer answer the internet. Any other Worker must answer 404.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_only_bindings_and_the_deployer_reach_a_recipe. cb2 2026-10-05 22:52 and cb4 2026-10-07 12:58: 404" },
  { id: "R21", status: "part", text: "Each call is an XRPC query or procedure. An error is { error, message }. Each method has a Lexicon.", check: "brain-core: test_routes_by_method_and_path. xrpc-client: test_xrpc_query_and_procedure. Not built: Lexicons; inputs are not checked against a schema" },
  { id: "R22", status: "built", text: "Each method and path has one rule, a CEL expression. The core must evaluate the rule before it forwards and must refuse when the result is not true.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_rules_are_cel_expressions, test_a_rule_that_does_not_parse_is_not_emitted. brain-core: test_a_rule_can_be_an_expression, test_owner_methods_refuse_other_callers" },
  { id: "R23", status: "built", text: "The owner can replace a rule with no deploy, unless the service fixed the rule.", check: "brain-core: test_the_owner_sets_a_rule_without_a_deploy" },
  { id: "R24", status: "built", text: "A Worker calls a method, never a Worker. The core must make the caller worker:NAME from the key, whatever headers the Worker sent.", check: "brain-core: test_a_worker_calls_a_method_not_a_worker" },
  { id: "R25", status: "built", text: "secret.put, token, grant, rule.put and infra methods must accept the owner's own session only. secret.get must accept the owner's own session, and a Worker that the rule of the secret lets in; it must refuse a turn token, an owner's token, a PDS and an anonymous caller.", check: "brain-kernel: test_infra_is_for_the_owner_session_only. brain-db: test_secrets_are_read_by_the_owners_session_and_by_a_worker_a_rule_names, test_db_only_the_owners_session_sets_a_rule. cb4 2026-10-07 08:40: the owner's turn token gets 401" },
  { id: "R26", status: "built", text: "A token or a grant reaches only the methods it names. It cannot name an infra, secret, token, grant or people method.", check: "brain-kernel: test_tokens_reach_only_their_methods, test_another_did_needs_a_grant, test_people_are_the_owners_to_change" },
  { id: "R27", status: "part", text: "The kernel must accept a service JWT from a PDS as its iss, after it checks aud, exp, lxm and the signature.", check: "brain-kernel: test_service_jwt_claims_are_checked_first. An experiment of 2026-10-05 on a scratch Worker. Not verified: a real PDS signature against this kernel" },
  { id: "R28", status: "built", text: "A Worker's key-value rows are its own. brain-db must decide a SQL statement that is not the owner's from its query plan, per table, and must refuse a plan with an opcode that is not listed.", check: "brain-core: test_notebook_rows_per_worker. brain-db: test_db_sql_decides_by_table_from_the_plan, test_db_sql_refuses_everything_when_the_plans_read_differently, test_db_a_table_is_open_to_whom_its_rule_says" },
  { id: "R29", status: "built", text: "A file or a blob is read and changed by tag. Only the store writes a by: tag or a worker: tag. A blob's address is the CID of its bytes.", check: "brain-static: test_static_a_files_tags_decide_who_reads_and_who_changes_it, test_static_only_the_owner_writes_the_shell. brain-blob: test_blob_tags_decide_who_reads_and_who_changes_it, test_blob_cid_is_the_cid_a_pds_gives_the_bytes. cb4 2026-10-07 13:12: 95 rows, 0 bad" },
  { id: "R30", status: "built", text: "The core must write one log line for each call that it answers or forwards, and the page must count them for the owner. Until 2026-10-09: the core counted calls and sent the counts to brain-metrics, which is removed.", check: "brain-core: test_one_log_line_a_call_with_these_keys_and_no_secret. cloud-brain: test_calls_from_the_logs_become_chart_rows. cb4: no db.sql by worker:brain-x-metrics in 10 minutes" },
  { id: "R31", status: "built", text: "Each event from outside reaches the page through the inbox: one entry per key, in order, kept until a tab marks it done.", check: "brain-inbox: test_inbox_once_per_key_in_order" },
  { id: "R32", status: "built", text: "One tab at a time holds the inbox lease. The lease ends 90 s after its last renewal.", check: "brain-inbox: test_lease_one_tab_at_a_time. Live: lease.get answers held: true" },
  { id: "R33", status: "built", text: "A turn must run as the sender of its entry, with a turn token. The turn must not reach more than the sender can call. The reply must go back on the entry's channel.", check: "brain-kernel: test_a_turn_is_made_as_its_sender, test_turn_token, test_poll_names_the_sender_and_hands_the_owner_turn_tokens. cloud-brain: test_turn_tool_calls_as_the_sender_or_not_at_all. brain-inbox: test_reply_goes_back_where_the_entry_came_from. cb4 2026-10-07 08:40 to 08:47" },
  { id: "R34", status: "part", text: "A turn in a room must reach inbox.reply and only the methods that each participant has a grant for.", check: "brain-kernel: test_a_room_turn_reaches_what_everyone_in_the_room_may_call, test_a_channel_can_narrow_a_turn_and_not_widen_one. cb4 2026-10-07 20:14: 74 rows. Not verified: a real group" },
  { id: "R35", status: "built", text: "When a turn fails, the page must mark the entry failed and tell the sender one time.", check: "cloud-brain: test_turn_failed_is_told_once_and_not_retried, test_turn_for_someone_not_added_runs_nothing" },
  { id: "R36", status: "part", text: "No Worker calls a model or runs an agent loop.", check: "review of the seeds, 2026-10-07: no service module calls a model. No test" },
  { id: "R37", status: "built", text: "A member deploy needs no approval. The Worker has one binding, to the core. It has no rows, secrets, paths, crons or methods open to anyone. Each call that it makes is checked as its author.", check: "brain-deployer: test_a_member_deploys_with_no_approval_and_only_the_core_bound, test_a_member_deploy_is_refused_outside_its_tier. brain-core: test_a_members_worker_calls_as_its_author_and_no_more. cb4 2026-10-07 12:58: 112 of 114 rows" },
  { id: "R38", status: "built", text: "A portal token must reach one member's methods as the viewer. The host page must not receive the member's module source.", check: "brain-kernel: test_a_portal_token_reaches_one_members_services_as_the_viewer. brain-shell: test_openPortal_frames_the_shell_and_answers_ready_with_a_token. cb4 2026-10-07 13:47: 69 rows" },
  { id: "R39", status: "part", text: "A channel must accept a message only from an address that is linked to a person, must check the service's signature where the service signs, and must append one entry per message id.", check: "brain-whatsapp: test_whatsapp_takes_signed_messages_from_linked_numbers, test_whatsapp_a_stranger_gets_a_link_and_no_entry. brain-bluesky: test_bluesky_a_person_is_served_and_a_stranger_is_told_once. WhatsApp round trip on cb4 2026-10-07 07:57. Bluesky on cb4 2026-10-07, inbox.list: entry 149 from the owner at 20:17 CEST and entry 164 from a member at 21:58 CEST, each done with one reply; bluesky.send answered sent: true 2 times. Not verified: the signature rule has no Bluesky case (Bluesky does not sign a message; the Worker polls with its own session), and a reply was not looked for in the Bluesky app" },
  { id: "R40", status: "part", text: "A copy of the page, a seed Worker address and an API token must install a Brain in that account and then delete the seed.", check: "cloud-brain: test_install_order_and_where_the_token_goes. cb2 2026-10-05 22:52: 32 s, in the same account. Not verified: a second account; the Clone form since the deployer began to distil (brain-db is not in the installer)" },
  { id: "R41", status: "part", text: "A Worker must call only the methods that its service lists in calls, and the three methods that a platform cell calls. The core must refuse any other call when the mode is enforce.", check: "brain-core: test_a_worker_calls_only_what_its_service_declared. cb4 2026-10-07: in mode report, a scratch Worker that declared lease.get called service.list (200) and static.get (400 from brain-x-static); both were counted. In mode enforce it got 200 on lease.get and 403 on service.list, static.get, secret.list and metrics.query. Under enforce the page loaded, the library saved, served and deleted a notebook, Bluesky polled, and no call was counted. Not verified under enforce: a WhatsApp picture (static.put) and a reply (inbox to *.send)" },
  { id: "R45", status: "built", text: "secret.copy must give a secret a second name with the same rule. The value must be in no answer. The new name must not be set. A member, a token, a Worker and a turn in a room must be refused.", check: "brain-db: test_a_secret_is_copied_to_a_new_name_and_its_value_is_in_no_answer. brain-kernel: test_a_room_turn_reaches_what_everyone_in_the_room_may_call. cb4 2026-10-07: 20 rows, 0 bad (.emitted/copy-live.ts, made-up values): the owner's session and an owner turn copy; a room turn, a member turn, a member session and a stranger get 403; no credentials get 401; a set name gets 409; no source gets 404; a BRAIN_ name gets 400; no answer holds the value" },
  { id: "R46", status: "part", text: "The signing key is SESSION_KEY. The kernel must read a token signed with SESSION_KEY or COOKIE_KEY. No name and no binding is removed.", check: "brain-kernel: test_the_signing_key_is_read_under_either_name. cb4 2026-10-07: the kernel has both bindings; a session made before the deploy is read after it. brain-deployer: test_the_signing_key_is_not_made_anew_under_its_new_name (a kernel deploy that is sent neither name keeps the held one and makes no value for the other). Not built: stage 2 (stop the write of the old name) and stage 3 (remove it)" },
  { id: "R47", status: "built", text: "A feed is a list of post URIs. feed.add must add 100 URIs at most in one call, must keep a URI one time, and must record the caller. A feed must keep 2000 posts at most and drop the oldest. app.bsky.feed.getFeedSkeleton must give a public feed to anyone, newest first, with a cursor. A feed that is absent or not public must answer UnknownFeed.", check: "brain-feed: each test of the module under simulate. cb4 2026-10-07: 5 real post URIs added, 0 added the second time; 2 pages of 2 and 3 posts with no sign-in; a feed that is not public answers 400 UnknownFeed; 2100 URIs leave 2000." },
  { id: "R48", status: "part", text: "feed.publish must write one app.bsky.feed.generator record in the repo of the Brain's Bluesky account, through brain-x-bluesky. bluesky.putRecord must refuse each other collection. feed.unpublish must delete the record.", check: "brain-feed: test_feed_publish_writes_the_record_through_the_bluesky_worker. brain-bluesky: test_bluesky_writes_only_a_feed_generator_record. cb4 2026-10-07: bluesky.putRecord answers 403 for app.bsky.feed.post. No record was written to a real account, and the Bluesky app was not seen to read a feed. feed.publish was not called on cb4 after the rule of bluesky.putRecord began to read origin (R50)." },
  { id: "R49", status: "built", text: "The kernel must pass a method outside com.lopecode.brain to the core as anonymous and must not read its token. /.well-known/did.json must name a #bsky_fg service of type BskyFeedGenerator.", check: "brain-kernel: test_a_method_of_another_lexicon_is_passed_on_as_anonymous, test_did_document_and_page. cb4 2026-10-07: describeFeedGenerator with a bearer that is not a JWT answered 401 before the change and 200 after it." },
  { id: "R50", status: "built", text: "A rule must be able to read origin: who started the chain of calls. For a call from outside, origin is the caller. For a call that a Worker makes while it answers a call, origin is the origin of the call that it answers. For a call that a Worker makes by its schedule, origin is the Worker. The core must sign the origin for one Worker with an end time, and must ignore a reference that is changed, ended, made for another Worker, or sent by the kernel. The wrapper must send the reference back with each call to the core (xrpc, secrets, sql, inbox), and two calls answered at one time must keep their own origin. bluesky.putRecord and bluesky.deleteRecord must refuse brain-x-feed when the origin is not the owner (origin.kind == \"owner\": the owner's tab, or a turn run for the owner).", check: "brain-core: test_the_origin_of_a_call_is_who_started_the_chain, test_a_reference_that_is_not_the_cores_own_gives_no_origin, test_a_members_worker_keeps_its_author_and_carries_an_origin. cloudflare-iac: test_the_wrapper_passes_the_origin_reference_on (under simulate a browser has no AsyncLocalStorage: two calls at one time pass no reference). brain-db: test_a_rule_reads_the_origin_the_core_names. brain-feed: test_feed_publish_writes_the_record_only_when_the_owner_started_the_chain. cb4 2026-10-07 23:25 to 23:26 CEST, scratch service brain-x-chaincheck, removed after: with no code to pass it on, the next method read origin owner/session for the owner and anonymous for no sign-in; a secret with the rule caller.worker == \"brain-x-chaincheck\" && origin.trusted was read for the owner and refused for no sign-in, in turn, inside 5 s; 3 rounds of 50 calls at one time (25 owner, 25 no sign-in), 150 calls, 0 with the origin of another call." },
  { id: "R51", status: "built", text: "The Worker that holds the Cloudflare token is named the deployer: the module @tomlarkworthy/brain-deployer, the Worker brain-deployer at BASE-deployer, the role and caller deployer, the cell deployer, the binding DEPLOYER, the header x-brain-deployer. A Brain from before the change must keep working and must be moved with no row deleted: the old spellings (BASE-guard with no config.self, the cell guard, the header x-brain-guard, the caller guard, \"guard\" in a rule, guardKey in the state file) must still be read. The page must learn the deployer's address from the kernel's DID document.", check: "brain-deployer: test_rows_move_to_a_deployer_that_holds_none, test_a_replaced_deployer_changes_nothing, test_the_deployer_binds_itself_under_its_own_script_name. cloudflare-iac: test_only_bindings_and_the_deployer_reach_a_recipe, test_rules_are_cel_expressions. brain-kernel: test_did_document_and_page. cb4 2026-10-07 23:52 to 23:58 CEST: 44 rows in 7 classes copied from cb4-guard to cb4-deployer, count and SHA-256 equal per class; 13 Workers deployed through cb4-deployer and each is same under redistil; the approval setting and the 2 held deploys are on it; cb4-guard answers 410 Replaced and its bindings are ROWS and BRAIN_CONFIG. Not verified: a Brain that stays on BASE-guard with this code for more than the 20 s of the move; the page of a signed-in owner after the move." },
  { id: "R54", status: "built", text: "With no tab that holds the lease, a channel must leave the message in the inbox and must tell that sender one time an hour that no tab is open.", check: "brain-whatsapp: test_whatsapp_no_tab_notice_once_an_hour_each. brain-bluesky: test_bluesky_no_tab_notice_once_an_hour_each. No run on a deployed Brain is recorded." },
  { id: "R52", status: "built", text: "A service is declared with cloudflare.Service(name, fn, options). cloudflare.Worker must stay the same function. A service is deployed as one Cloudflare Worker, in the wrapper.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_a_service_declared_with_the_old_name_emits_the_same (the manifest is equal; worker.js differs in that one word, so the hash differs). cb4 2026-10-07 23:25 CEST: a scratch service declared with cloudflare.Worker was distilled and deployed by the new deployer. 16 declarations in the seeds use Service." },
  { id: "R53", status: "part", text: "The deployer page must show, for each held deploy, each method and path with who may call it, the calls the service declares, and the secrets it names. A rule that reads origin must be marked.", check: "brain-deployer: test_approval_holds_an_apply. cb4 2026-10-07: the 2 held deploys of brain-x-whatsapp are from before this change and show 'not recorded' for rules and calls. A deploy held by the new deployer was not seen on cb4." },
  { id: "R55", status: "built", text: "A service must reach Cloudflare Browser Run only through the platform cell browser. The deployer must bind a browser to a service that reaches the cell, must say so on the approval page, and must refuse the cell to a member's service. The change must not alter the emitted code of a service that does not reach the cell.", check: "brain-deployer: test_a_browser_is_bound_shown_before_approval_and_not_for_a_member. cloudflare-iac: test_bindings_follow_platform_cells. cb4 2026-10-08: after the deployer update, redistil gave same for each of the 13 Workers; brain-x-browser deployed with the binding" },
  { id: "R56", status: "built", text: "A browser must be the pair of its owner and its name; the owner is the caller that the core names, and no parameter names an owner, so a caller reaches its own browsers and no others. Each browser must be one Browser Run session with its own paidUntil and its own end. The name is default when absent. browser.all and browser.end, which reach the browsers of each owner, must be for the owner's own session by a rule the owner cannot change. The owner must be able to limit the browsers that are up, in all and for one owner. browser.open must open a page with a name as a tab of the browser, in a browser context of its own, and must give the same tab for the same name. The row of a page must hold no credential. open, goto and run must refuse an address that is not http or https, a local name and a private address.", check: "brain-browser: test_browser_each_caller_has_its_own_browsers, test_browser_declares_what_it_needs, test_browser_open_makes_a_tab_and_reuses_it_by_name, test_browser_each_call_is_a_new_connection_to_the_same_tab, test_browser_refuses_urls_and_too_many_pages. cb4 2026-10-08: the owner had browsers a and b and the Worker brain-x-bruser its own; the Worker got 401 from all and end and reached no page of the owner; close of a left b answering" },
  { id: "R57", status: "built", text: "Browser time must be bought before it is used, by browser.extend alone: seconds in the query string, a whole number from 10 to 3600, added to the paidUntil of the browser that the call names, or to now when that has passed. extend must be the one method with a price, seconds × 0.000025 US dollars, and the price must be 0 for a seconds that the service refuses, so that what is charged is what is added. Purchases made at one time must all count. A method that uses the browser with no time bought must answer 409 NoTime and name browser.extend. Time that is bought must not be given back. The service must have no spending limit of its own. When the time has passed, the browser must be closed by the next call or tick, whatever tabs are open.", check: "brain-browser: test_browser_time_is_bought_by_extend_alone, test_browser_price_is_what_extend_adds, test_browser_gives_no_time_that_was_not_bought. cb4 2026-10-08: see the as-built record" },
  { id: "R58", status: "built", text: "browser.eval must give the value, or what the page threw, and must stop at its timeout. browser.run must close its tab when the job ends, throws or runs out of time. No CDP command may wait on a promise of the page.", check: "brain-browser: test_browser_eval_gives_a_value_or_what_the_page_threw, test_browser_text_screenshot_logs_and_goto, test_browser_run_closes_its_tab, test_browser_run_stops_at_its_timeout. cb4 2026-10-08: run on example.com gave Example Domain in 1831 ms cold and 665 ms warm; no session was left" },
  { id: "R59", status: "part", text: "A browser that ends or stops answering must not make a call wait past 10 s, and its pages must answer PageClosed with the reason. The service must close only the sessions it has a row for: a session that a dead start left, and a session of a different Worker, are not closed by the tick.", check: "brain-browser: test_browser_tick_makes_rows_and_sessions_agree, test_browser_that_stops_answering_is_closed. cb4 2026-10-08: 3 tabs of the Brain's page stopped the browser two times; a call then waited until its client gave up at 30 s. The 10 s limit was added after that and was not seen to work on cb4" },
  { id: "R63", status: "built", text: "A method or a path of a service may answer a WebSocket upgrade with status 101. The wrapper of each Worker, the kernel and the core must pass that answer on with its socket. The caller must be identified, the calls list checked, the rule decided and the price charged at the upgrade, as for a call with one answer. A caller on the internet must not be able to name itself on an upgrade.", check: "cb4 2026-10-08, tools/scratch/ws-probe/hops.ts and checks.ts: before the change each upgrade answered 500 (Responses may only be constructed with status codes in the range 200 to 599); after it, 101 as the owner's session, a token, and a Worker by its own key through the core; 401 by the rule for no caller; 403 for a call the Worker did not declare; a price of 0.0001 was charged; a forged x-brain-caller header arrived as anonymous; frames of 33 MB passed each way; one socket was held 10 minutes. No test guards the two lines that pass the socket on (stamp in cloudflare-iac, the CORS middleware in brain-kernel): a tab cannot make a Response with status 101" },
  { id: "R64", status: "built", text: "browser.cdp must give the caller the Chrome DevTools Protocol socket of the caller's own browser, as Browser Run gives it, with no frame read or changed. It must need bought time, must start the browser when it is down, and must answer 426 to a GET that is not an upgrade. The socket must close when the browser ends.", check: "brain-browser: test_browser_cdp_is_the_socket_of_the_callers_own_browser. cb4 2026-10-08, tools/scratch/ws-probe: playwright-core connectOverCDP did goto, a click with a wait for the navigation, trusted key events and a screenshot; raw Runtime.evaluate p50 60.7 ms against 427 ms for browser.eval; the Worker brain-x-wscdp got its own browser by its own key; a socket closed 13.3 s after paidUntil, which an extend had moved while it was open" },
  { id: "R65", status: "built", text: "The deployer must turn Workers Logs on for each Worker and Cloudflare's own line per invocation off, because that line stores request headers and the whole URL. It must set this on a script that is already deployed. With that line off Cloudflare still stores the method and URL of the call, with its query string, beside each line a Worker writes: a long-lived secret must not be in a path or a query string.", check: "brain-deployer: test_every_upload_turns_logs_on_and_the_invocation_line_off. cb4 2026-10-08 18:57 UTC: each of the 17 cb4 scripts had logs enabled with invocation_logs false; a query for lines of type cf-worker-event, and for the text x-brain-deployer and authorization, each found 0. Not verified: that no header can reach a line through an error message" },
  { id: "R66", status: "built", text: "The core must write one log line for each call, with these keys and no others: at, ray, caller, via, origin, method, worker, status, error, ms, price, rule, by. The line must hold no header, no body, no value of a parameter and no secret. The kernel must pass the cf-ray of a call to the core, and the core to the Worker.", check: "brain-core: test_one_log_line_a_call_with_these_keys_and_no_secret, test_the_log_line_of_a_priced_call_has_its_price. cb4 2026-10-08: a 401 had rule deny, by manifest; a 402 had error OutOfCredits and price 0.0015; the lines of the core and of the service of one call had the same ray and the same Cloudflare trace id" },
  { id: "R67", status: "built", text: "A service must write a log line with the platform cell log, which adds the Worker's name and the ray of the call and lets the service set neither. The wrapper must write one error line when a service throws. The deployer must write a line for each step of a deploy with its reason, and the browser service a line for each browser that starts and ends with the reason.", check: "cloudflare-iac: test_log_writes_the_workers_name_and_the_ray_and_the_ray_goes_on. brain-deployer: test_the_deployer_logs_each_step_of_a_deploy_and_why_it_was_put_back. cb4 2026-10-08: deploy.put-back with Cloudflare's message 'Uncaught Error: boom at start'; browser.start, then browser.end with reason 'time ran out' after 99 s; a throw line with the name RangeError and the stack" },
  { id: "R68", status: "built", text: "A service may declare Cloudflare permission groups (cloudflare: [GROUP]). The deployer must hold such a deploy for the owner also when deploys need no approval, must refuse it for a member, for a role other than recipe and for a group not in its list (Workers Observability Read, Workers AI Read), must mint an account token of exactly those groups that ends in 90 days, must bind its value to that Worker alone and keep only its id, groups and end, and must write an audit row for each mint, roll and delete. The same groups on a new deploy must keep the token while more than 30 days are left. Other groups must give a new token and delete the old one. A service removed must delete its token. A version put back must get a token that works. The wrapper must give a service the cloudflareApi cell only when it declares a group.", check: "brain-deployer: test_a_declared_cloudflare_permission_is_held_for_the_owner_and_minted_for_that_worker_alone, test_a_cloudflare_permission_is_refused_off_the_list_and_outside_a_recipe, test_a_version_put_back_gets_a_token_that_works. cloudflare-iac: test_cloudflareApi_needs_a_declared_permission_and_sends_the_bound_token. cb4 2026-10-08 18:51 UTC: one token, 'cb4-x-logs: minted by cb4-deployer', one group, to 2027-01-06; a token of the same policy was refused script settings, script content, secrets, D1 and a mint. Not verified on cb4: a roll, a changed set, a removal, a put-back, and the approval page for this service (the deploy was by the recovery key)" },
  { id: "R69", status: "built", text: "logs.query, logs.keys and logs.values must pass a body to Cloudflare's telemetry API and return its answer as it is, errors included. They must put the caller's filters inside a filter on the script names of this Brain, which no parameter removes; ?worker=NAME must narrow that filter to one Worker of this Brain. The rule must be the owner's own session unless the owner sets another. The page must have a Logs panel for the owner.", check: "brain-logs: test_a_query_is_passed_on_inside_this_brains_filter, test_worker_narrows_a_query_to_one_worker_of_this_brain, test_logs_declares_one_cloudflare_permission_and_the_owners_session. cloud-brain: test_logs_panel_asks_cloudflare_and_a_row_filters_by_its_trace. cb4 2026-10-08: a scratch Worker read 4 lines of its own script and got 401 for brain-core, by the owner's rule; a line was readable 11.4, 14.1 and 15.9 s after its call; the panel's code, with a client on cb4, showed 13 lines of status 400 and above, and a click on one gave the 4 lines of its trace from 2 Workers. Not verified: the panel in the signed-in page of cb4, and that a queryId of a saved query cannot widen a query" },
  { id: "R60", status: "built", text: "A method or a path may have a price: one CEL expression over caller, origin and request that gives US dollars. The owner must be able to set a price in place of the declared one, in the owner's own session only. A call with no price must write no row. A price that throws, is not a number or is less than 0 must refuse the call; a price above the most for one call must refuse it.", check: "brain-core: test_a_call_with_no_price_writes_nothing, test_a_price_that_cannot_be_decided_refuses_the_call, test_the_owner_sets_prices_and_allowances_in_their_own_session. cb4 2026-10-08 07:25 CEST, core ea6aa69af073, scratch service removed after: 0.002 charged 0.002; double(request.params.seconds) * 0.000025 with seconds=40 charged 0.001 and with no seconds answered 403. A price declared in a manifest reaches the core since 2026-10-08 (brain-browser: test_browser_declares_what_it_needs)." },
  { id: "R61", status: "built", text: "The core must charge a priced call to the account of its origin before it forwards the call, and must refuse the call with 402 OutOfCredits when the account has less than the price left for the UTC day. A call with no account must be refused. Calls made at one time must not spend past the allowance. The owner sets an allowance in the owner's own session; an account reads its own day.", check: "brain-core: test_the_origin_pays_through_one_worker_and_through_two, test_out_of_credits_is_402_and_nothing_is_forwarded, test_calls_made_at_once_do_not_spend_past_the_allowance, test_a_new_day_starts_at_nothing_and_old_days_are_dropped, test_a_members_worker_spends_its_authors_credits. cb4 2026-10-08: 150 calls of $0.03, 50 at one time, on an account with $1.00: 33 answered 200 and 117 answered 402, spent 0.99. A call through 1 Worker and through 2 Workers was charged to the owner at each priced method. Not seen on cb4: a member, a turn, a Worker by its own clock." },
  { id: "R62", status: "built", text: "A priced call must be charged when the core accepts it, and the charge must not be returned, whatever the Worker answers (Tom, 2026-10-08: \"Don't do refunds that complicates thing, we want small lean code\"). Each charge must be one row of a ledger the owner reads, kept 30 days.", check: "brain-core: test_a_charge_is_not_returned, test_a_priced_call_is_charged_to_the_day_of_its_origin, test_a_new_day_starts_at_nothing_and_old_days_are_dropped. Until 2026-10-08 a failed call was given back and a Worker could lower its charge with x-brain-cost; both were removed. The delete of a day older than 30 days ran under simulate only, with a moved clock." },
  { id: "R42", status: "not built", text: "A Worker must call a method on another atproto service as the owner, through the kernel and the owner's PDS.", check: "from a Worker: a query to did:web:api.bsky.app#bsky_appview returns the owner's profile" },
  { id: "R43", status: "not built", text: "The owner must be able to read the status, duration and error of the last 100 requests to a Worker and replay one in the tab.", check: "after a request that throws, the trace shows the message; the replay under simulate throws the same message" },
  { id: "R44", status: "not built", text: "A relay must carry pairing frames between a page on a phone and a Claude Code session.", check: "the page on a phone, paired from a laptop: list_cells returns" }
]
// %%
requirementsTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th>id</th><th>requirement</th><th>status</th><th>check</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${requirements.map((r) => htl.html`<tr data-requirement=${r.id}><td><strong>${r.id}</strong></td><td>${r.text}</td><td>${r.status}</td><td>${r.check ? htl.html`<span style="font-size:.9em">${r.check}</span>` : htl.html`<em>none</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
// %%
design = md`## Decisions

Each row is in force. **words** quotes the person who decided. A row with no quote is Claude's choice and is not confirmed.

| | decision | who, when, words |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | The assistant runs in a tab. A Worker is a stateless service. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "we can't really run the Observable runtime meaningfully in a worker, therefore all runtime stuff has to be done in the tab" |
| A2 | A service is declared from a function. Its ancestor cells are emitted as a plain module. A Cloudflare resource is a platform cell. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "it will need to chase ancestors a bit like notebook distiller. No generators." |
| A3 | A service is tested in the tab with simulated requests. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "We will need to simulate requests in the tab so we can unit test them outside of deployment." |
| A4 | The inbox is the one path from outside to the assistant. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "The inbox pattern becomes a central concept." |
| A5 | Each Worker reports its own version. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "can we insist all workers have a metadata route" |
| A6 | Hono is the router. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "I assume the core router will be Hono" |
| A7 | XRPC is the convention for each call, inside the Brain and from outside. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "xrpc is then perhaps the backbone" |
| A8 | Approval of deploys is a setting. It is on at install. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "Some people want HITL and some do not."; "safe defaults but with easy loosening" |
| A9 | Install goes through a seed Worker that the installer pastes in the Cloudflare dashboard. | Tom, 2026-10-04: "people can't run shells though in general" |
| A10 | A separate deployer deploys and watches, and holds the only token. The Brain cannot change the deployer. | Claude; not objected to |
| A11 | One owner DID, set at install. | Tom, 2026-10-05: "yes 1 owner" |
| D1 | A service is one package under one hash: source, code, manifest, tests. A deploy is the save. | Claude, 2026-10-06; not objected to |
| D2 | A Worker serves its module source and its manifest. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "module source plus manifest" |
| D3 | A service's source is readable by anyone. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "lets go with public for now" |
| D4 | The page is one more service. Assistant sessions are not part of a package. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "cloudbrain should jsut be another service" |
| D6 | A probe is a normal test cell. The page runs the tests from the deployed module and reports. A clear failure restores the previous version. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "A clear fail (no absence of callback) would trigger an instant rollback when in the unverified state." |
| D7 | The Worker is the source of truth. A deploy is module source. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "I think the worker is the source of truth" |
| D8 | The deployer distils in QuickJS. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "I think it would need a quickJS solution, which is honestly safer in the guard anyway" (the deployer was called the guard until 2026-10-07) |
| D9 | The deployer holds what a distil needs: \`cloudflare-iac\`, the runtime, the parser, \`hono.js\`, \`cel.js\`. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "All those heavy things seem only used by the guard?" |
| D10 | An import of a Brain module resolves to the source of the Worker that owns the module. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "the page is rendering from the workers also itself" |
| D11 | The shell is a file in \`brain-static\`. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "Maybe serve shell from blob storage or whatever we have at the moment." |
| D12 | Only the owner writes the shell. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "yes only owner writes it" |
| D13 | The shell does not contain the Workers' modules. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "shell should load without the workers code" |
| D14 | Metrics have their own SQL tables. | Tom, 2026-10-06: "it should have its own table." |
| D15 | All SQL goes through \`brain-db\`, checked per table from the query plan. The core stays on \`rows\`. | Tom, 2026-10-07; no words recorded |
| D16 | Roles are owner and member. The owner can grant a member more methods. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "the roles would be "owner" and "member", and we might want to grant extra permissions per person." |
| D17 | Each person is an atproto account. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "Everyone needs an atproto account." |
| D18 | The owner reads each conversation. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "Yes I can read everyones conversations coz I am the owner." |
| D19 | A failed turn is marked failed and the sender is told one time. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "Mark failed, tell the sender once" |
| D20 | No agent loop in a Worker. A turn with no tab open needs a notebook in a container. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "Don't build the serverside loop, we want to reuse notebooks" |
| D21 | A turn runs as its sender. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "we need to give the whats app handler the ability to "assume identity" or something." |
| D22 | The Brain answers in group chats. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "I think it should be able to participate in group chats though." |
| D23 | A session is a bearer token in \`localStorage\`. The kernel uses no cookie. | built 2026-10-07 13:20; who decided is not in the build record |
| D24 | The page has a docs tab. The operator is told to read it. | Tom, 2026-10-07: "We should have a cloud-brain-docs tab by default that explains what you can do and the technical design. The operator should also be prompted to read it." |

Replaced, with what replaced it:

| was | by |
|---|---|
| The tab saves a notebook as a bundle of SHA-256 blobs, and a deploy reads the saved bundle (Tom, 2026-10-04) | D1, D7, D11 |
| Only deployed code runs on Cloudflare; no Worker holds an interpreter (Tom, 2026-10-04) | D8: the deployer interprets module source to distil it |
| One notebook file holds each service module | D10, D13: the shell loads them from the Workers |
| The kernel keeps a cookie session | D23 |
| A deploy compares hashes of code emitted in the tab | D7: the deployer distils; the hash is of the source and the distiller version |
| The owner's number is linked by a code | each person links an address the same way, at \`/link\` |`
// %%
md`### Platform facts

Measured on Cloudflare, 2026-10-04 to 2026-10-07.

| fact | consequence |
|---|---|
| A Durable Object's memory is gone after 30 s idle | no state in a Worker's memory |
| \`eval\` and \`new Function\` fail at request time | a Worker runs distilled code; the deployer interprets in QuickJS |
| A version at 0% answers a request that has a version override | the deployer tests a version before go-live |
| A rollback by the deployments call is healthy in 2.7 s | restore is automatic |
| The Cloudflare API refuses a browser preflight | the seed Worker |
| The deployer's cron trigger did not run on 2026-10-05 | the deployer ticks from an alarm |
| \`workers.dev\` is on the Public Suffix List | sibling addresses are one site; no cookie session |
| A distil takes 131 ms of CPU at p50; the Free plan allows 10 ms | the deployer needs the paid plan |
| Chromium does not run a cross-origin frame that is off screen | Open scrolls to the portal frame |

Not checked: a Free-plan install; a blob near 50 MB; the Bluesky cron over hours.`
// %%
handover = md`## Handover

### Where the work is

- **Seeds**: \`tools/cloud-brain/*.ojs\`, one per module. \`bun tools/cloud-brain/build.ts\` writes \`lopebooks/notebooks/@tomlarkworthy_cloud-brain.html\` and the shell.
- **This module**: \`cloud-brain-specs.ojs\`. The build adds the notes and the status from the previous build, then the short build record from \`spec-as-built-short.md\`. The full working record is \`spec-as-built.md\`; the build does not put it in the page.
- **CLI**: \`tools/cloud-brain/brain.ts\` (\`install-deployer\`, \`apply\`, \`confirm\`, \`redistil\`, \`shell\`, \`session\`, \`curl\`, \`bindings\`; \`migrate-deployer\` and \`retire-guard\` for a Brain from before 2026-10-08). It is a test harness and is not part of the product.
- **Live Brain**: \`cb4\`. Backlog: \`plan/cloud-brain-backlog.md\`.
- **Not committed as of 2026-10-08**: \`tools/cloud-brain/\` and \`plan/cloud-brain-backlog.md\` are in no git commit. \`tools/cloud-brain/.emitted/\` is ignored by git: it holds keys, emitted services and one-off check scripts, and a check that this spec cites from it is on one machine only.

### Boundaries

| | |
|---|---|
| **always** | run the module's tests before a deploy; deploy to scratch Worker names; record times from the clock |
| **ask first** | a new npm dependency in the deployer; a change to \`exporter-3\`, \`robocoop-5\` or \`lopecode-channel.ts\`; a message to a person |
| **never** | give a Worker other than the deployer a Cloudflare token; run a model call in a Worker; let \`secret.get\` or \`infra.*\` accept a token or a service JWT; let an owner apply touch a name outside \`brain-x-\`; print a key, a session or a token |

### Checks

\`\`\`
bun tools/cloud-brain/build.ts
bun tools/cloud-brain/test-receiver.ts                      # serves run-tests.js on 127.0.0.1:47814
# in a paired tab: run(["<module>", ...]) from http://127.0.0.1:47814/run.js
BRAIN_BASE=cb4 bun tools/cloud-brain/brain.ts redistil      # each Worker: same
BRAIN_BASE=cb4 bun tools/cloud-brain/brain.ts curl /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.lease.get --owner
\`\`\`

### Known traps

- A hidden tab computes nothing. The lease must end when a tab stops.
- A cell is emitted as its source, not its value. A constant runs again in the deployer's sandbox.
- A deployed service has unrestricted outbound network access.
- A rollback of code does not roll back rows or tables.
- \`did:web\` is the hostname. A Brain that changes hostname is a new service and a new OAuth client.
- The seed is an open relay to the Cloudflare API until the installer deletes it.
- An open tab runs the page it loaded. Reload it after a page deploy.
- A service JWT proves who, not which app. The kernel's OAuth scope is \`transition:generic\`.`
