  "q": "Defaults, by choice of Claude where you gave none: owner $1.00 a day, member $0.10, a Worker by its own clock $0.10, a token $0.10 (an account of its own, not the owner's), at most $1 for one call, at most 2000 priced calls a day for one account. Change any?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "A turn in a room is charged to the person who wrote the message, as any turn is, because the kernel names that person as the caller. The others in the room pay nothing. Is that who should pay?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "A cost known only after a call (the tokens of a model call) is not built. A price is fixed before the call, and since 2026-10-08 nothing brings a charge down afterwards (x-brain-cost was removed with the refunds). It needs a design of its own: a price that is the most the call can cost, or a second priced call that the Worker makes for what was used. Which, when a model call gets a price?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "quota.get shows an account its own day. Only the owner reads the list and the ledger. Should a member see what other members spent?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Deployer rename, stage 2 (R51). The Worker is still brain-deployer at BASE-deployer. A new Worker name is a new Worker with an empty Durable Object: the rows (each Worker's key and kept source, the held deploys, the approval setting) must be copied, the approval address changes, and each Worker bound to DEPLOYER is deployed again. The caller id deployer is in rules (who: \"workers\"). Do stage 2, and when?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": "Done on cb4, 2026-10-07 23:52 to 23:58 CEST. Tom, 2026-10-07: \"2 yes\", and before that \"do it slowly without deleting anything\". The Worker is cb4-deployer. cb4-guard is a stub with no token and no key; its rows are as they were. Open: when to delete cb4-guard."
 },
 {
  "q": "The origin now reaches the rule of each secret and table. No rule on cb4 reads it there. Should a rule of inbox *.send, static.put or a secret read origin? Claude changed none.",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "cloudflare.Worker is the old name of cloudflare.Service (R52) and has no other meaning. Is a bare Worker, with no wrapper and no manifest, wanted later under that name?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Feed URI match: does getFeedSkeleton compare the account in the feed URI?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": "Closed 2026-10-07, confused-deputy review. Yes. A feed answers only for the URI that feed.publish recorded: the account, the collection app.bsky.feed.generator, and the name. A different URI, or a feed that is not published, answers UnknownFeed. Before, a record in a different account that named this Brain got the posts of a public feed under that account. The owner reads a feed that is not published with feed.posts."
 },
 {
  "q": "Browser service: is the assistant to have a tool for it? It has none. A page reads text from any address, and that text would come into the assistant's turn.",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Browser service: three tabs of the Brain's own page stopped one browser on cb4 (2026-10-08, two attempts of two; two tabs reached about 800 MB of heap). A page with a browser of its own (open with own: true) was built and then removed on 2026-10-08 with the refunds, for less code: one browser, one paidUntil. When a Brain is hosted, is each hosted page to have a browser of its own again, at one browser-hour each?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": "Yes, by a name. Tom, 2026-10-08: \"its a shared service, each browser will be owned by another process, so this one thing has to serve the whole cluster. Of course there will need to be multiple browsers, please fix.\" A browser is now the pair of the caller that owns it and a name, each with its own Browser Run session and paidUntil. On cb4 the same day, two tabs of the Brain's page in one browser ended it and the one tab in a second browser still answered."
 },
 {
  "q": "Browser service: time that is bought and not used is not given back, and a browser with time left and no page stays up until paidUntil. Is that the wanted rule, or is close of the last page to end the browser?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": "Not given back. Tom, 2026-10-08: \"Don't do refunds that complicates thing, we want small lean code\". Time is bought by browser.extend alone; close of the last page leaves the browser up until paidUntil, which is the smaller code."
 },
 {
  "q": "No charge is returned by the core (R62). If the owner must be able to return one by hand (a service charged for something it did not do), the smallest form is one owner-session method that appends a credit against a ledger id. Not built. Wanted?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Browser service: settings and liveView are for the owner's own session and their rule is fixed. A token cannot change the limits or get a link that controls a tab. Is that right?",
  "blocking": false,
