  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Logs: the core's line holds the caller and the origin as they are (a DID, token:NAME), kept 7 days by Cloudflare. Tom, 2026-10-08, to 'a line records the caller's identity': yes. A token with Workers Observability Read reads the lines of each Worker on the Cloudflare account, and logs.query limits a query to this Brain by a filter in the service, not by the token. Accept, or wait for a token for each Worker (Cloudflare has such roles; not tried)?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
 {
  "q": "Logs: the kernel has an uncaught TypeError, 'Can't read from request stream after response has been sent', on a POST that the core refuses before it reads the body (seen in the logs for a 401 and a 402, cb4 2026-10-08). The caller gets the right answer. It is one error line for each such call. Fix in the kernel (read or cancel the body), or leave?",
  "blocking": false,
  "answer": ""
 },
